Throne & Liberty Build Analysis

Objective

Investigate the trade-off between poison-based gameplay and sustained pressure gameplay.

Hypothesis

Traditional builds overinvest in poison mechanics.

Testing Areas

Damage consistency
Resource management
Skill synergy
Rotation complexity
Build accessibility

Key Finding

Players often achieve greater consistency through sustained-pressure gameplay loops than highly specialized poison rotations.

Skills Demonstrated

Combat Design
Balance Analysis
Player Decision Making
Gameplay Flow

Aion 2 Combat Rework Case Study

Problem
Aion 2's extensive use of macros reduced meaningful player interaction and lowered the skill ceiling of combat.

Developer Response
NCSoft redesigned combat systems to reward manual gameplay and reduce the effectiveness of macros.

Community Reaction
Korean community responses generally fell into several categories:

Supporters of higher skill expression
Players concerned about increased complexity
Players dissatisfied with class-specific changes
Players who felt the changes did not go far enough
Design Lessons
The strongest reactions centered around:

Agency
Build expression
Class identity
Reward structures
Skill expression
Conclusion
Player engagement appears strongly linked to meaningful decision-making rather than passive optimization.
